      "created_at": "2012-08-28T13:21:00.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Assuming you're not referring to our individual number of posts (which do not appear to be displayed) but to the new posts showing up correctly, yep, all good!  <img src=\"//forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/sunglasses.png?v=9\" title=\":sunglasses:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":sunglasses:\"></p>\n<p>(And I'm okay not showing individual post counts, as I think it motivates people to post more in ways that are not necessarily useful or productive, but that's just my opinion.  <img src=\"//forums.greaterthangames.com/images/emoji/apple/wink.png?v=9\" title=\":wink:\" class=\"emoji\" alt=\":wink:\"> )</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Thanks, Joel!</p>",
